        "original_id": "8b306567-d00e-5342-8e7e-6bcc983d0ef3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Angelique Kerber, Amélie Mauresmo, Andrea Petkovic, Victoria Azarenka\n- Events: 2015 Family Circle Cup – Singles, 2004 Summer Olympics\n- Topics: WTA rankings, Grand Slam singles titles\n\nFacts:\n- Amélie Mauresmo was born on 5 July 1979 and became a French former professional tennis player and former world No. 1.\n- Amélie Mauresmo won two Grand Slam singles titles at the Australian Open and Wimbledon.\n- Amélie Mauresmo won a silver medal at the 2004 Summer Olympics.\n- In the 2015 Family Circle Cup – Singles, defending champion Andrea Petkovic lost to Angelique Kerber in the semifinals.\n- On 12 September 2016, Angelique Kerber reached world No. 1.\n- Angelique Kerber became the twenty-second player and the oldest player to reach world No. 1 for the first time.\n- Angelique Kerber was the first new world No. 1 player since Victoria Azarenka in 2012.",
